{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795220,"nonce":"PX3+U4D0TctRZRGJTOUMzHeJHlg=","title":"Implement asynchronous RayScript network and provider credential services","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P0\n\nScope\nImplement the services Jam/providers need beyond the current placeholder net.fetch/process.spawn declarations: asynchronous HTTPS and WebSocket operations, optional controlled helper launch, streaming responses, cancellation, deadlines and bounded incoming/outgoing queues. Define capability/endpoint scopes, redirect/token handling, credential-broker handles and lifecycle ownership. Bind sockets/fibers/requests to extension/session lifetime and native host wakeups. Provide headless extension fixtures for reconnect and worker failure.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nBlocked/slow DNS, TLS, network I/O and process launch never wait in a UI handler. Unmount, disable, reload, sign-out and late replies release work safely. Unauthorized endpoints/operations fail with a useful error; logs redact secrets. Signed-out/no-Jam idle adds no polling. Native faults and queue overload are contained according to the existing host model.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}